date-released: '2026-11-09'
abstract: We present the philosophical basis and research programme of a generative framework for
  mathematics and physics. The central question concerns the origin of the objects, assumptions,
  and operations from which a theory begins. Logical consistency constrains their consequences but
  does not establish their correspondence with nature. Taking minimal unbiased change as the common
  starting point, the framework studies how relations close into ordered structures and how successive
  levels acquire their own objects and laws. The main argument develops this view from the discussion
  in Beyond Apparent Paths. Three appendices develop the physical, mathematical, and engineering
  pictures that guide the programme. A common source connects internal spectra, gauge and matter
  structure, a positive equilibrium Yang–Mills gap, collective gravity, and cosmic evolution. Retaining
  the formation of numbers and functions supplies history-dependent responses, a signed scale-energy
  approach to the Riemann hypothesis, and a study of efficient generation and verification. For the
  Navier–Stokes equations, finite evolutions with controlled residuals, stability, and spectral tails
  are completed into continuum solutions on certified intervals. The unifying aim is to trace the
  starting points of these problems to a common process of generation and to retain that process
  in their mathematical description.
